  "description": "36-Hour Hackathon | VIBRANT 2K26: Build • Innovate • Impact The 36-Hour Hackathon is a flagship technology event under VIBRANT 2K26, organized by Vibeesta Creative Society & Shrinik Club, G.L. Bajaj Institute of Technology and Management. Participants will compete through multiple stages, demonstrating their technical knowledge, innovation, problem-solving skills, and ability to build practical solutions for real-world challenges. Eligibility: Open to college students across India. Students from any academic discipline can participate. Each team must consist of 2–4 members. A participant can be part of only one team. All participants must provide accurate registration details. Competition Format: Round 1 — Online Assessment: Participants will take an online assessment testing technical knowledge, logical reasoning, aptitude, and problem-solving skills. Qualified teams will advance to Round 2. Round 2 — PPT Submission: Qualified teams will submit a PPT presenting their proposed solution. The PPT should cover: Problem Statement. Proposed Solution. Innovation / USP. Technology Stack. Feasibility. Expected Impact. Scalability. Selected teams will advance to the offline hackathon. Round 3 — 36-Hour Hackathon: Shortlisted teams will participate in the 36-hour offline development challenge. Teams will: Ideate → Build → Test → Refine → Submit → Demo.",
